title: frontier_clerk
---
<<present_speaker "npc_frontier_clerk">>
<<if verdict("encounter.cleared", "frontier.marshal_gallus") == "satisfied">>
    Dolores: Name, origin, cargo. Sorry. I say it even when I recognize people.
    -> The Marshal is beaten.
        Dolores: I heard the whistle stop. I have a queue of people asking whether they still owe him twelve credits.
        Dolores: The toll box is still in his office. I'm recording arrivals in a separate book until we find out who has a right to collect.
        Dolores: Ruth asked whether I could pay the night crew out of it. I told her I couldn't just start spending money from the toll box myself.
    -> ‹go›
<<elseif verdict("encounter.cleared", "frontier.marshal_gallus") == "unanswerable">>
    <<stop>>
<<elseif verdict("world.flag_set", "frontier_clerk_met") == "satisfied">>
    Dolores: Still logged. Still here. Pad Three, arrivals.
    -> Who gets the toll?
        Dolores: Gallus. Twelve credits a head, through the gate or off a ship. I have to put the receipts in his box.
        Dolores: He used to have authority to collect it. Nobody here has seen his new warrant. The box still goes to his office.
    -> ‹go›
<<elseif verdict("world.flag_set", "frontier_clerk_met") == "not_satisfied">>
    <<command "world.set_flag" "frontier_clerk_met" true>>
    Dolores: Hold it. Arrivals sign in.
    Dolores: Name, origin, cargo.
    -> I came through the gate.
        Dolores: Origin: gate. Cargo: none. Fine.
        Dolores: Gallus will want his toll. He's got men watching the arrivals.
    -> ‹say nothing›
        Dolores: Origin: unknown. That's allowed. I've logged worse.
<<else>>
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
===
title: frontier_liveryman
---
<<present_speaker "npc_frontier_liveryman">>
<<if verdict("world.flag_set", "frontier_liveryman_met") == "satisfied">>
    Gus: Mules by the day. Same price as yesterday.
    -> Why not something with an engine?
        Gus: Dust gets in an engine on the pass and the engine stops. A mule stops too, but you can argue with a mule.
    -> ‹go›
<<elseif verdict("world.flag_set", "frontier_liveryman_met") == "not_satisfied">>
    <<command "world.set_flag" "frontier_liveryman_met" true>>
    Gus: If you want a horse, I don't have one. Don't ask me again.
    -> I didn't ask.
        Gus: You were going to. Folks look at me and they think I've got cousins out back.
        Gus: Mules. Six of them. My sister shoes them and I do the rest.
    -> ‹say nothing›
        Gus: Mules by the day, then. Bring the same number of legs back.
<<else>>
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
===
title: frontier_barkeep
---
<<present_speaker "npc_frontier_barkeep">>
<<if verdict("encounter.cleared", "frontier.marshal_gallus") == "satisfied">>
    Mae: First glass of water's on the house. Three of the night crew came in together, and for once nobody got up to listen for the whistle.
    -> How are they doing?
        Mae: Tired. They put their money together for one pot of coffee. I sent three cups and told them to come back after the meeting with Ruth.
    -> ‹go›
<<elseif verdict("encounter.cleared", "frontier.marshal_gallus") == "unanswerable">>
    <<stop>>
<<elseif verdict("world.flag_set", "frontier_barkeep_met") == "satisfied">>
    Mae: Water's two. Coffee's three.
    -> Tell me about the Marshal.
        Mae: He drinks here at noon. Coffee, black. He sometimes comes in with a coyote. That one pays his own tab. Gallus tells me to put it down to the Marshal's office.
        Mae: When he's mad he goes to the corral and shoots at cans. When he's very mad he whistles.
        Mae: Don't be in the yard when he whistles.
    -> ‹go›
<<elseif verdict("world.flag_set", "frontier_barkeep_met") == "not_satisfied">>
    <<command "world.set_flag" "frontier_barkeep_met" true>>
    Mae: Welcome to the Whistle. You look dry.
    -> What's good?
        Mae: Water. It came eleven hundred miles on a tanker, so it's the best thing on the shelf.
        Mae: The blue stuff is coolant. Somebody drinks it every month.
    -> ‹say nothing›
        Mae: Suit yourself. The stool's free.
<<else>>
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
===
title: frontier_prospector
---
<<present_speaker "npc_frontier_prospector">>
<<if verdict("world.flag_set", "frontier_prospector_met") == "satisfied">>
    Elias: Still here? Sit down, sit down.
    -> Where's the lead?
        Elias: In the creek, if you believe me, and nobody does. Lead in the gravel, grey as a bad tooth.
        Elias: The refinery pays by the pound. Gallus has been taking his cut before I get to the weigh station.
    -> What happened to the Marshal?
        Elias: Accident at the cracking tower, back when he was a plain rooster on a plain farm. So they say.
        Elias: Then the company built him back up out of the parts they had. I'd have asked for fewer guns.
    -> ‹go›
<<elseif verdict("world.flag_set", "frontier_prospector_met") == "not_satisfied">>
    <<command "world.set_flag" "frontier_prospector_met" true>>
    Elias: You're new. Good. Everybody else has heard all of it.
    Elias: Forty years in this pass. Panned every creek from here to the far pads. Found lead.
    -> Lead?
        Elias: Lead! I used to sell a bag or two a week. Now they want to know where I found it.
    -> ‹say nothing›
        Elias: That's fine. I'll talk for both of us.
<<else>>
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
===
title: frontier_foreman
---
<<present_speaker "npc_frontier_foreman">>
<<if verdict("encounter.cleared", "frontier.marshal_gallus") == "satisfied">>
    Ruth: I stopped the carts after the fight. We had two men out on the terrace who hadn't slept.
    Ruth: I've called the morning crew in at seven. I'm going to ask them what hours they can actually work.
    -> What about their pay?
        Ruth: Dolores has the toll accounts. I asked if we could use that money for the night crew. She wants proper authority first. Fair enough. I still have to face the crew at seven.
    -> ‹go›
<<elseif verdict("encounter.cleared", "frontier.marshal_gallus") == "unanswerable">>
    <<stop>>
<<elseif verdict("world.flag_set", "frontier_foreman_met") == "satisfied">>
    Ruth: Hat on, or off the terrace.
    -> What does the Marshal want?
        Ruth: Ore in the carts. Nobody on the road after the whistle. His toll, his cut, his rules on a board.
        Ruth: He still acts like he runs the place. Four in the morning, even when the carts are backed up and there's nowhere to put the ore.
    -> How do I get to the corral?
        Ruth: Up the road past the tower. Mind the chickens on the way.
    -> ‹go›
<<elseif verdict("world.flag_set", "frontier_foreman_met") == "not_satisfied">>
    <<command "world.set_flag" "frontier_foreman_met" true>>
    Ruth: You're on my terrace without a hard hat.
    -> Sorry.
        Ruth: Mind the chickens, then. They're his. They don't swerve.
    -> I'm going to the corral.
        Ruth: To see the Marshal? He'll see you first. The road goes up past the tower.
        Ruth: If you get him to lie in past four, the whole shift owes you a drink.
<<else>>
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
===
title: frontier_station_agent
---
<<present_speaker "npc_frontier_station_agent">>
<<if verdict("world.flag_set", "frontier_station_agent_met") == "satisfied">>
    Augusta: Tickets for the gate on the left of the window, tickets for the train on the right. Same window.
<<elseif verdict("world.flag_set", "frontier_station_agent_met") == "not_satisfied">>
    <<command "world.set_flag" "frontier_station_agent_met" true>>
    Augusta: Off the gate? Sit on the bench a minute before you walk anywhere.
    Augusta: The inn's up the street if the bench isn't enough. Most people need the inn.
<<else>>
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
<<jump frontier_station_agent__topics>>
===

title: frontier_station_agent__topics
---
-> Is this the main terminal?
    Augusta: This is the auxiliary. The main pads are at Dry Dock, down the line. We get the overflow and the detours.
    <<jump frontier_station_agent__topics>>
-> When's the next train?
    Augusta: The Number 9 goes down the gulch at 9:40. It's freight. It doesn't stop for people.
    <<jump frontier_station_agent__topics>>
-> Does Hettie get her parts by train?
    Augusta: When she can. She brings me the part numbers herself. If a crate comes in with only her name on it, I send it to the workshop unopened.
    <<jump frontier_station_agent__topics>>
-> ‹go›
===
title: frontier_innkeeper
---
<<present_speaker "npc_frontier_innkeeper">>
<<if verdict("world.flag_set", "frontier_innkeeper_met") == "satisfied">>
    Pearl: Lie down or move along, dear. The cots are for lying down.
    -> Where are Alice and Bob?
        Pearl: The cots by the window. Try not to open the curtains all at once.
    -> ‹go›
<<elseif verdict("world.flag_set", "frontier_innkeeper_met") == "not_satisfied">>
    <<command "world.set_flag" "frontier_innkeeper_met" true>>
    Pearl: Welcome to the Lie-Down. A cot by the hour, a bucket with every cot.
    -> I'm a robot. I don't get gate-sick.
        Pearl: Then you can carry buckets. No, I'm teasing. Your friends are by the window.
    -> ‹go›
<<else>>
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
===
title: frontier_inn_alice
---
<<present_speaker "npc_alice">>
<<if verdict("world.flag_set", "frontier_inn_alice_met") == "satisfied">>
    Alice: Still here. Bob's just managed to sit up. We'll be a while yet.
<<elseif verdict("world.flag_set", "frontier_inn_alice_met") == "not_satisfied">>
    <<command "world.set_flag" "frontier_inn_alice_met" true>>
    Alice: This isn't where we meant to come out. The dialer back home only had the one line working after the bear.
    Alice: Bob and I need about an hour before we can set off again. We'll look at the routes to the city when we can read a map without feeling worse.
<<else>>
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
-> Where is the mechanic?
    Alice: Across the trestle on Sprocket Row. That bear knocked you about; ask the mechanic to check your joints.
-> I'll wait with you.
    Alice: Thanks. Could you put that bucket between the cots? Bob says he's fine. He's gone a funny colour.
-> ‹go›
===
title: frontier_inn_bob
---
<<present_speaker "npc_bob">>
<<if verdict("world.flag_set", "frontier_inn_bob_met") == "satisfied">>
    Bob: Tell Alice I'll be up in a minute. On second thoughts, make that ten.
    -> ‹go›
<<elseif verdict("world.flag_set", "frontier_inn_bob_met") == "not_satisfied">>
    <<command "world.set_flag" "frontier_inn_bob_met" true>>
    Bob: I told Alice I'd carry the instruments this time. I barely got them as far as the inn.
    Bob: Halfway Siding. I've got the name written down at least. I'll ask Alice to check the spelling when she's feeling better.
    -> ‹go›
<<else>>
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
===
title: frontier_mechanic
---
<<present_speaker "npc_frontier_mechanic">>
<<if verdict("world.flag_set", "frontier_mechanic_met") == "satisfied">>
    Hettie: Back again. Anything rattling?
<<elseif verdict("world.flag_set", "frontier_mechanic_met") == "not_satisfied">>
    <<command "world.set_flag" "frontier_mechanic_met" true>>
    Hettie: Hettie Gimbal. Pumps, windmills, wagons, the odd automaton. What's broken?
<<else>>
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
-> Could you check my joints?
    Hettie: Turn round. Lift that foot. Hm. A dent, a scuff, nothing loose. You're fine.
    Hettie: If it starts rattling under load, bring it back before it drops off. Saves us both work.
-> What do you work on here?
    Hettie: Mostly the pumps and wagons. See that spring? Came off a freight wagon. Been waiting two weeks for its replacement. Augusta checks for the crate every time a train comes in.
    Hettie: I could ask her to open the other boxes and look, but she is quite right not to do that.
-> ‹go›
===
title: frontier_brakeman
---
<<present_speaker "npc_frontier_brakeman">>
Hollis: Where did you come from? Never mind. That isn't our engine up front.
Hollis: Something coupled on at the head of the train in the night. The engine crew jumped off at the water stop. The train just kept going.
Hollis: Keep off the couplings. If you fall between the cars, you're under the train.
-> ‹go›
===
title: frontier_yardmaster
---
<<present_speaker "npc_frontier_yardmaster">>
<<if verdict("world.flag_set", "frontier_yardmaster_met") == "satisfied">>
    Lou: The tipple road goes up to the works. The street goes under it to the Row. Both come out at the railhead.
<<elseif verdict("world.flag_set", "frontier_yardmaster_met") == "not_satisfied">>
    <<command "world.set_flag" "frontier_yardmaster_met" true>>
    Lou: You came off the Number 9. At speed. I saw that.
    Lou: That engine's been through four times this month and taken cars every time. Nobody in this yard is going to stand on the line and argue with it.
<<else>>
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
-> Where am I?
    Lou: Clinker Flats. The smelter town. Dry Dock's east along the line, past the railhead.
-> ‹go›
===
title: frontier_crane_driver
---
<<present_speaker "npc_frontier_crane_driver">>
<<if verdict("world.flag_set", "frontier_crane_driver_met") == "satisfied">>
    Magda: Keep off the pots. I'm not fishing you out of the slag.
    -> Do you live near the works?
        Magda: Near enough. I leave a clean shirt with Ida before a shift so I have something to change into. She says I ought to make the manager do his own washing for a week.
    -> ‹go›
<<elseif verdict("world.flag_set", "frontier_crane_driver_met") == "not_satisfied">>
    <<command "world.set_flag" "frontier_crane_driver_met" true>>
    Magda: I tip the slag pots from up there. Forty a shift, if the crane doesn't stick. It sticks worse in the cold.
    Magda: You're standing where the ladle swings, by the way.
    -> ‹go›
<<else>>
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
===
title: frontier_laundress
---
<<present_speaker "npc_frontier_laundress">>
<<if verdict("world.flag_set", "frontier_laundress_met") == "satisfied">>
    Ida: Same as yesterday. Wash it at noon, the works lets out soot at one, wash it again.
<<elseif verdict("world.flag_set", "frontier_laundress_met") == "not_satisfied">>
    <<command "world.set_flag" "frontier_laundress_met" true>>
    Ida: Mind the lines. That's the whole night shift's shirts. The bundles with a red thread are for the smelter crew.
<<else>>
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
-> Why live under the works?
    Ida: The wind can't get in, the rent's low, and the soot's free.
-> Who leaves clothes with you?
    Ida: Magda brings me a clean shirt before work and takes a clean one home after. I wash the dirty one. The works manager pays me by the piece and never asks why she needs two a day.
-> ‹go›
===
